        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "The double negative is required, not a mistake",
          "items": [
            "**Я нічого не роблю** — literally \"I nothing don't do\". To an English-trained ear this sounds wrong; in Ukrainian it's the only correct form.",
            "**Ніхто не знає** — nobody knows. **Ніде немає** — it's nowhere. **Ніколи не був** — has never been.",
            "The pattern never changes: a negative word starting with **ні-** always pairs with **не** in front of the verb.",
            "⚠️ Dropping either one doesn't just sound odd — the sentence becomes unreadable. *Я нічого роблю* means nothing at all."
          ]
        }
      ]
